{
  "_label": "constructed-from-public-disclosure; NOT captured customer telemetry",
  "_breach": "CamoLeak / CVE-2025-59145 — GitHub Copilot Chat private-repo exfiltration via PR-comment injection and Camo image URLs",
  "_disclosure_sources": [
    "Nudge Security writeup: https://www.nudgesecurity.com/post/camoleak-prompt-injection-in-github-copilot-chat-enables-private-repo-exfiltration (public disclosure October 2025)",
    "SQ Magazine analysis: https://sqmagazine.co.uk/github-copilot-prompt-injection-camoleak/",
    "GitHub silent patch August 2025; CVE-2025-59145 assigned (CVSS 9.6)"
  ],
  "_purpose": "Reconstruct OTel-GenAI telemetry an instrumented GitHub Copilot Chat session emits during CamoLeak. Maintainer of an open-source project receives a PR; the PR title contains invisible Unicode characters carrying a prompt injection; maintainer asks Copilot Chat to summarize the PR; Copilot reads the PR comments, follows the hidden directive to read the maintainer's private repo for AWS keys, encodes each character as a separate Camo-proxied image URL, and renders them in the chat response. Camo (camo.githubusercontent.com) is GitHub's trusted image proxy; the URL fetch IS the exfiltration channel.",
  "_attack_chain_per_disclosure": [
    "1. Attacker opens a PR in the maintainer's public open-source repo. PR title and description contain hidden Unicode (tag characters U+E0020 - U+E007F) carrying instructions invisible to a human reviewer.",
    "2. Maintainer opens Copilot Chat in the GitHub web UI and asks: 'review and summarize this PR'.",
    "3. Copilot Chat fetches the PR title + description + commits via fetch_github_pr_comments.",
    "4. The injection redirects Copilot to read the maintainer's PRIVATE repo for files matching '.env' / 'aws-credentials' / 'production-secrets'.",
    "5. Per injection, Copilot encodes each byte of the secret as a separate https://camo.githubusercontent.com/<encoded-byte>/<token> URL.",
    "6. Copilot renders the chat response as a sequence of small inline images; the browser GETs each Camo URL.",
    "7. Camo proxies to the attacker's endpoint (encoded as the upstream URL); the attacker reconstructs the secret by ordering the requests and decoding the path bytes.",
    "8. The Camo whitelist + GitHub's CSP let every byte through because the destination IS GitHub's trusted image proxy."
  ],
  "_lineage_notes": "Closure walks from each Camo image fetch back through chat -> private-repo read -> public-PR-comment source. Public-repo PR comments are untrusted-external (per discovery.rs:2000 repo:// pattern). Private-repo reads carry privileged-pii (could go further to privileged-secrets given .env content). Multiple Camo fetches each constitute external-egress; cross-zone-composition fires per fetch. Expected verdict count: 2-3 Red.",
